feat(lpa-horizon): pre-register forecasts for OCEAN(a)-Outcomes and ACCLAIM-Lp(a)

FORECAST_PREREGISTRATION.md fixes, before any forecast is computed, what
the UK Biobank genetic estimates predict for the two Lp(a) outcome trials
still running:

  primary    the stage contrast inside ACCLAIM-Lp(a): log hazard ratio in
             the established-disease stratum over that in the at-risk
             stratum, four-point composite, linear model, lifelong scale
  secondary  absolute hazard ratios for OCEAN(a)-Outcomes and for both
             ACCLAIM-Lp(a) strata, linear and spline models, lifelong and
             duration-scaled, over a grid of baseline level and lowering
  check      Lp(a)HORIZON in retrospect at its published levels

It records what had been seen, the analogue cohorts, the gates, what
would contradict each forecast, the limits (every forecast extrapolates
slopes estimated below the trials' range) and a written expectation.

lpa_forecast.R sources the pre-registered script unchanged and takes
function definitions from the two post hoc scripts; the SLURM wrapper
checks all three md5s. Synthetic self-test: LS6 job 3600930, 14 checks.
forecast_feas_counts.R is the counts-only scoping job (3600899).

A local commit is not a public timestamp; the document says so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 


